 "result": "Use `@needs_app_scope`, defined at `src/tessel/cli.py:380`. It wraps the callback so it runs inside the app context.\n\n- **Decorator:** you often don't need to apply it yourself. Registering with `@app.cli.command()` (or any `AppGroup.command`, `src/tessel/cli.py:405`) wraps the function in `needs_app_scope` automatically. Pass `needs_app_scope=False` to opt out.\n- **Class that loads the app:** `LaunchInfo` (`src/tessel/cli.py:293`). Its `load_app()` method at `src/tessel/cli.py:333` is what `needs_app_scope` calls (line 397) to get the app.\n- **Related:** `TesselGroup` (`src/tessel/cli.py:531`) is the top-level CLI group. It uses `LaunchInfo.load_app()` to discover app-registered commands.",
